From 3e17670cf5c55897f9610cc58aedaaceccdee992 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:24:29 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 171/171] wsi/x11: pick the sw readback memory type per
 swapchain from its frame rate

Whether the cached readback type (with a full-frame invalidate) or the
uncached one is faster depends on the workload, not on the frame size: on
the X6 Pro (v11), with the same 640x360 swapchain, the D3D11 cube runs 382
fps cached vs 271 uncached, but D3D11 FL 11_1 505 vs 708. The per-arch
default of 0168/0169 can only win one of them.

With MIT-SHM and the deferred reply (the sw present path of 0160), each
BUFFER_BLIT swapchain now measures its mean frame interval in the starting
mode, the other mode and the starting mode again (A, B, A), each window at
least 120 frames and 500 ms after a 30 frame / 250 ms settle, starting 1 s
after the first present. It switches if B is 3 % faster than the mean of the
A windows, then holds, and measures again when the interval drifts by 25 %
(at most every 10 s). wsi_image_set_cpu_readback_cached() moves one image
to the other type right after its CPU copy, while it is idle.

The arch default stays the starting mode. PANVK_WSI_SW_CACHED=0/1 forces a
mode and disables the measurement.

X6 Pro, PanPlay, auto vs 122e cached / uncached (fps): D3D11 cube 352 and
383 vs 370 / 271; D3D11 FL 11_1 753 and 709 vs 562 / 759; D3D9 118 vs 118
/ 118. Build 116: cube 312-333, FL 11_1 404-443.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
